From: aignis <6974796+aignis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:08:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] switch2: own main() with SD logs and a large game stack,
 lifecycle events, fatal screen

switch2_main.c redirects stdout/stderr next to the NRO, runs the game on an
8 MiB stack thread, and main.c shows a console message when the game data is
missing instead of returning to hbmenu. The SDL subset reports HOME/sleep as
SDL background/foreground events so the game pauses audio and rebases its
VBlank clock.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
